ived ≥1 JYNNEOS vaccine dose\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n \"conditions\": [\n  {\n   \"v\": \"monkeypox\",\n   \"role\": \"outcome\",\n   \"ev\": [\n    {\n     \"loc\": \"title\",\n     \"q\": \"Incidence of Monkeypox Among Unvaccinated Persons Compared with Persons Receiving ≥1 JYNNEOS Vaccine Dose\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"v\": \"monkeypox\",\n   \"role\": \"vaccine target\",\n   \"ev\": [\n    {\n     \"loc\": \"text\",\n     \"q\": \"was approved by the Food and Drug Administration (FDA) in 2019 to prevent smallpox and monkeypox infection\"\n    }\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"study_design\": [\n  {\n   \"v\": \"surveillance/descriptive\",\n   \"ev\": [\n    {\n     \"loc\": \"text\",\n     \"q\": \"Monitoring monkeypox incidence by vaccination status in timely surveillance data might provide early indications of vaccine-related protection\"\n    }\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"data_source_type\": [\n  {\n   \"v\": \"CDC surveillance system\",\n   \"ev\": [\n    {\n     \"loc\": \"figure 1\",\n     \"q\": \"number of probable or confirmed cases reported to CDC\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"loc\": \"text\",\n     \"q\": \"separately submit deidentified vaccine administration data to CDC\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"v\": \"vaccination registry\",\n   \"ev\": [\n    {\n     \"loc\": \"text\",\n     \"q\": \"or link cases with vaccination data from their immunization registries\"\n    }\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"data_source_named\": [\n  {\n   \"v\": \"CDC Atlas Plus\",\n   \"ev\": [\n    {\n     \"loc\": \"note\",\n     \"q\": \"jurisdiction-specific estimates of 2020 HIV prevalence are from CDC’s Atlas Plus\"\n    }\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"setting\": {\n  \"v\": \"US subnational\",\n  \"ev\": [\n   {\n    \"loc\": \"title\",\n    \"q\": \"32 U.S. Jurisdictions, July 31–September 3, 2022\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n \"vaccine_outcome_type\": {\n  \"v\": \"effectiveness\",\n  \"ev\": [\n   {\n    \"loc\": \"summary\",\n    \"q\": \"These early findings suggest that a single JYNNEOS dose provides some protection against monkeypox infection.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n \"equity\": {\n  \"level\": 0,\n  \"level_reason\": \"Sex, age and MSM status only define the analyzed population and the vaccine-eligible denominator; no results are reported by any social-position group.\",\n  \"level_confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"level_alternative\": {\n   \"level\": 1,\n   \"reason\": \"The introduction notes the outbreak disproportionately affected MSM, but this is background, not an analysis.\"\n  },\n  \"dimensions\": [\n   {\n    \"v\": \"sex\",\n    \"role\": \"population\",\n    \"basis\": \"assigned or observed\",\n    \"ev\": [\n     {\n      \"loc\": \"note\",\n      \"q\": \"Cases reflect infections occurring among persons who self-reported sex assigned at birth or self-reported gender identity as male.\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"v\": \"sexual orientation and gender identity\",\n    \"role\": \"population\",\n    \"basis\": \"self-identified\",\n    \"ev\": [\n     {\n      \"loc\": \"note\",\n      \"q\": \"Cases reflect infections occurring among persons who self-reported sex assigned at birth or self-reported gender identity as male.\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"loc\": \"figure 1\",\n      \"q\": \"Gay, bisexual, and other men who have sex with men who have HIV infection or who are eligible to receive HIV preexposure prophylaxis\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"v\": \"age\",\n    \"role\": \"population\",\n    \"ev\": [\n     {\n      \"loc\": \"text\",\n      \"q\": \"The analysis was limited to males aged 18–49 years to exclude persons who might have received routine smallpox vaccination in childhood.\"\n     }\n    ]\n   }\n  ],\n  \"determinants_of_health\": {\n   \"v\": null,\n   \"ev\": []\n  },\n  \"equity_action\": {\n   \"v\": false,\n   \"ev\": []\n  },\n  \"equity_measurement\": \"The eligible-population denominator is MSM with HIV or eligible for HIV-PrEP (a behavior-based definition); no SPD strata are analyzed.\"\n },\n \"groupwise\": [],\n \"uncertain_fields\": [\n  \"analytic_depth\",\n  \"study_design\"\n ],\n \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n \"notes\": \"The average IRR is a ratio of population-weighted average weekly incidences, which is arithmetic, not survey weighting. Two sensitivity analyses (a wider eligible-population denominator; assuming 50% or 100% of unknown-date cases were vaccinated ≥14 days earlier) gave lower IRRs. No design is named; surveillance/descriptive is inferred. Unknown vaccination status was assumed unvaccinated.\",\n \"view_issues\": \"Second-dose case counts are given as of September 23, outside the stated study window.\"\n}", "type": "text"}]}